@cc [label:security] allowed-visualization-origins
`ALLOWED_VISUALIZATION_ORIGIN` is the comma-separated list of front origins allowed to embed viz.
The content page must reject `postMessage` events from any other origin, and the `frame-ancestors`
CSP directive must include the configured exact origins in development and production. Production
configuration must accept only HTTPS origins; development may also accept HTTP origins. Invalid,
non-origin, credential-bearing, or wildcard values must fail config evaluation. Existing Dust and
browser-extension ancestors remain allowed independently of this variable.
